# SuperHabits — Project Rules

## Project identity

SuperHabits is an offline-first React Native + Expo app rendered as a **single-page experience**: the six sections (Overview, Todos, Habits, Pomodoro, Workout, Calories) are rendered inside `app/index.tsx` behind a `NavigationContext.activeSection` state with a top tab rail of plain `Pressable` items. Settings is a full-screen **modal** (not a route); the Command Center is a **global overlay** only (mounted by `GlobalCommandCenterHost` in `app/_layout.tsx`). There are no `/settings`, `/command`, or `/(tabs)/*` routes.
Stack: React Native 0.83.4, Expo 55, TypeScript 5.9, expo-router, SQLite
(expo-sqlite WAL mode), NativeWind 4, Vitest.
Target: Web (PWA), iOS, Android.
Status: Active MVP. **Web PWA** can be deployed to **Vercel** using root `vercel.json` (`npm run build:web` → `dist/`, COOP/COEP headers, SPA rewrites).
Current stored schema version: **11** (see `app_meta.db_schema_version`). Next migration: add a new **`if (version < 12) { ... }`** block in `runMigrations()` in `core/db/client.ts` when a schema change lands.

Current product-shell facts to preserve:
- The command center is a **global overlay** only; `/command` is not a route anymore.
- Calories supports `Form` and `Diary` modes and remembers the last selected view.
- Settings is organized into six sections: Appearance, Backup / Sync / Restore, AI / Command, Notifications / Timer defaults, Nutrition defaults, Developer / Internal.
- Remote backup wording must stay conservative: push backup plus restore v1 preview/import, not full two-way sync.

## Non-negotiable invariants — violating these causes silent data corruption

1. SOFT DELETE ONLY
   Never use DELETE FROM on main entity tables (todos, habits, habit_completions
   is the exception, workout_logs, calorie_entries, pomodoro_sessions).
   Always set deleted_at = datetime('now') and filter WHERE deleted_at IS NULL.
   Hard delete = data loss with no recovery path.

2. SYNC ENQUEUE ON EVERY WRITE
   Every INSERT/UPDATE on main entities must call syncEngine.enqueue(record)
   immediately after the DB operation.
   Exceptions (intentionally not synced): pomodoro_sessions, workout_logs,
   habit_completions.
   Missing enqueue = silent sync gap when cloud sync is enabled.

3. DB SINGLETON MUST INITIALIZE BEFORE ANY DATA ACCESS
   All data functions call await getDatabase() at the start.
   Never open a second SQLite connection. Never access db before init.
   Breaking the singleton breaks the entire app on cold start.

4. IDs VIA createId(prefix) ONLY
   Never use Math.random(), crypto.randomUUID(), or raw timestamps as IDs.
   Format: {prefix}_{timestamp}_{random8} — enforced in lib/id.ts.
   Prefix must match the entity: "todo", "habit", "cal", "wrk", "pom".

5. DATE KEYS VIA toDateKey() ONLY
   All YYYY-MM-DD date strings must come from toDateKey() in lib/time.ts.
   Since migration 5, toDateKey() uses the device’s **local** calendar date
   (YYYY-MM-DD). Rows written before migration 5 used UTC calendar dates;
   see `app_meta.date_key_cutover` — no silent backfill of old rows.

6. MIGRATIONS ARE APPEND-ONLY AND MONOTONICALLY INCREASING
   Never modify an existing migration. Always append a new `if (version < N) { ... }`
   block in `runMigrations()` in `core/db/client.ts` — there are no numbered migration
   files. Current stored version: 11; the next block is `if (version < 12)`.
   schema.sql is a reference doc only — it is NOT executed at runtime.

7. UNIQUE(habit_id, date_key) on habit_completions
   The data layer (habits.data.ts) avoids duplicate rows by:
   - SELECT for an existing row matching (habit_id, date_key)
   - INSERT with createId("hcmp") if none exists; UPDATE count if it does
   - On decrement to zero: DELETE that row (hard delete — allowed exception for this table)
     Do not change this pattern without reviewing UNIQUE and sync implications.

## File naming conventions

- Source files: camelCase (e.g. todoHelpers.ts)
- React components: PascalCase (e.g. TodoCard.tsx)
- Data layer: {feature}.data.ts (e.g. todos.data.ts)
- Domain/pure logic: {feature}.domain.ts (e.g. habits.domain.ts)
- Screens: {Feature}Screen.tsx (e.g. TodosScreen.tsx)
- Sections render inside app/index.tsx behind the top tab rail — no per-feature route files

## Adding a new feature — required structure

features/{name}/
{name}.data.ts ← all SQLite CRUD, exports typed functions
{name}.domain.ts ← pure logic, no DB imports, fully testable
{name}Screen.tsx ← React Native UI, imports from .data and .domain

Route file: app/index.tsx → add the section to the tab rail + render it behind `NavigationContext.activeSection`
Tab entry: app/index.tsx → add a Pressable to the top tab rail

## Unused dependencies — do NOT add usage without discussion

The following are installed but intentionally unused:

- date-fns (listed in package.json, not imported anywhere in source)

`zustand`, `@tanstack/react-query`, `expo-background-fetch`, and `expo-task-manager`
are **not** installed — do not add them without an explicit decision.
Do not wire these up without an explicit decision to do so.

## Testing requirements

- Every new \*.domain.ts function must have a Vitest unit test
- Test files live in tests/ directory
- Run: npm test
- Baseline: `npx vitest list` shows the current inventory (630 tests as of the last full pass); the gate is **0 failures** on `npm test` — never maintain a magic total count in this file
- Data/DB, restore, linked-actions, and provider-model tests already exist. Component rendering tests are still limited — document that gap honestly instead of describing the suite as domain-only.

## E2E Tests (Playwright)

E2E tests live in `e2e/` at the project root. They run against the **static web export** in `dist/`, served by `node scripts/serve-e2e.js` on `http://localhost:8081` with `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` (OPFS + SQLite WASM). **Playwright does not build the app:** run `npm run build:web` yourself whenever React components or web bundle output change, then run E2E. Metro (`npm run web`) is for local dev with HMR — **not** used by the E2E pipeline.

**Test files:**

- `e2e/todos.spec.ts` — Todos feature
- `e2e/habits.spec.ts` — Habits feature
- `e2e/pomodoro.spec.ts` — Pomodoro feature
- `e2e/workout.spec.ts` — Workout feature
- `e2e/calories.spec.ts` — Calories feature
- `e2e/settings.spec.ts` — Settings backup/restore surface
- `e2e/command.spec.ts` — Command-center launcher and confirm-before-write flow
- `e2e/command.eval.mock.spec.ts` / `e2e/command.eval.internal.spec.ts` — command draft quality/evaluation coverage
- `e2e/command.observation.mock.spec.ts` / `e2e/command.observation.internal.spec.ts` — command observation/fallback coverage
- `e2e/boundary.spec.ts` — cross-feature boundary and regression cases
- `e2e/infrastructure.spec.ts` — Headers, SW, OPFS, DB init
- `e2e/theming.spec.ts` — theme switching/contrast coverage
- `e2e/journeys/*.spec.ts` — cross-feature user journeys (the `journeys` project; its `@sync` steps also run as the opt-in `journeys-sync` project)

**Config:** `playwright.config.ts`

- `headless: true` always
- Chromium only
- `workers: 1` locally (do not increase — OPFS + expo-sqlite hold one lock per origin; extra workers cause flaky navigation/reload). `fullyParallel: false` — tests in a file stay serial; `clearDatabase()` in `beforeEach` must not race.
- `webServer.command`: `node scripts/serve-e2e.js` (serves `dist/`; ensure `npm run build:web` has been run)
- `retries: 2` on CI, `0` locally
- HTML report: `.cursor/playwright-output/e2e-report/`
- Failure screenshots / traces: `.cursor/playwright-output/e2e-failures/` (`outputDir`)

**Commands:**

- `npm run e2e` — run all E2E tests (chromium + journeys + simulation projects; baseline 181 tests in 19 files — compare against `npx playwright test --list`, 0 failures is the gate)
- `npm run e2e:sync` — opt-in `journeys-sync` project (`@sync` steps) against the `dist-sync/` build on :8082; main/nightly only, not part of the default `npm run e2e`
- `npm run e2e:report` — open HTML report
- `npm run e2e:headed` — run with visible browser (debug only)
- `npm run e2e:debug` — Playwright inspector

**Slash commands:**

- `/test` — run unit tests + E2E tests in one pass
- `/e2e-fix` — run E2E, read report via Playwright MCP, auto-fix

**E2E invariants:**

- `clearDatabase()` called in `test.beforeEach` (not `afterEach`)
- `e2e/global.setup.ts` aborts if `crossOriginIsolated` is false
- Do not add `data-testid` to app components
- Do not change assertions to make tests pass artificially
- If a test reveals a genuine bug, fix the app not the test
- E2E tests are NOT unit tests — they require the static server (or CI’s `build:web` + `npm run e2e`)

## CI (GitHub Actions)

Three jobs (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`; lane matrix enforced by `validateMatrix()` in `simulation/matrix.ts`):

- **quality** — typecheck + lint + unit tests (runs first, on every trigger)
- **e2e** — runs after **quality** on PRs and main pushes (and manual `workflow_dispatch`): the PR lane runs the chromium suite + P0 journeys + simulation validation/deterministic subset; the main lane runs the full `npm run e2e`, the full deterministic simulation library, a `dist-sync/` build, and `npm run e2e:sync` (the `journeys-sync` project)
- **nightly** — schedule-only, non-gating: full `npm run e2e` + seeded simulation lane + `dist-sync/` build (+ optional disposable-backend lane when `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` is configured)

## Current known bugs (do not silently fix — coordinate first)

- Sync flush is gated on `isRemoteEnabled()` (`lib/supabase.ts`) — interval / visibility / NetInfo flush
  runs when remote is enabled (**default `remoteMode` is `"enabled"`**). If `setRemoteMode("disabled")` is used,
  flush listeners are not registered and the in-memory queue can grow — intentional local-only tradeoff.
  The exported `syncEngine` uses **`SupabaseSyncAdapter`** (push upsert); if Supabase env vars are unset,
  `supabase` is `null` and pushes no-op without throwing. Document as tradeoff, not a silent bug fix.
- schema.sql is out of date (reference only, not authoritative)

Resolved in repo (do not re-report as open): CaloriesScreen passes user-selected `mealType` to `addCalorieEntry` (meal type picker); `syncEngine.flush()` is wired in `AppProviders` when `isRemoteEnabled()` is true; **`ensureAnonymousSession()`** runs on bootstrap when Supabase is configured. **toDateKey()** now uses local calendar dates (migration 5 records `date_key_format` / `date_key_cutover` in `app_meta`).

Implementation note: `nextPomodoroState` in `features/pomodoro/pomodoro.domain.ts` is covered by Vitest; **PomodoroScreen** currently uses inline button labels and does not import it — wire the screen to the domain helper if you want a single source of truth for `Running...` vs `Start focus`.

## Web / PWA context (not application bugs)

- **COEP / COOP:** `metro.config.js` and `app.json` set isolation headers for dev; production static web on **Vercel** uses root **`vercel.json`** (`Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp`, `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin`, SPA rewrite `/(.*)` → `/index.html`) so `crossOriginIsolated` holds for SQLite WASM on web.
- **Service worker:** `public/sw.js` uses cache name `superhabits-shell-v3` (`CACHE_VERSION = "v3"`). **Dev bypass:** requests to `localhost` / `127.0.0.1` use network-first `fetch` (no stale Metro cache).

## MCP tools (development)

Configured in the user’s MCP settings (e.g. `~/.cursor/mcp.json` on Unix; equivalent on Windows). Useful servers for this repo:

- **Playwright MCP** — live browser inspection; use with `/pre-pr` and `/e2e-fix`.
- **Lighthouse MCP** — performance, PWA, accessibility; use with `/audit-performance`.
- **Fetch MCP** — HTTP header verification (e.g. COOP/COEP); use in `/audit-performance` phase 1.

**Slash commands (summary):** `/pre-pr`, `/audit-performance`, `/test` (unit + E2E), `/e2e-fix` (E2E run + report-driven fixes).
